    <text type="letter">
        <body>
            <div type="writingSession">
                <pb n="1"/>
                <opener><dateline><date when="1950-02-06">February 6,
                        1950</date></dateline><salute>Dear <rs type="person"
                            ref="#tillich_person_id__5496">Mrs. Williams</rs>:</salute>
                </opener>
                <p>You are in a sharp competition with the Book Department of the Chicago Press. If
                    I had to review the two books to which you refer now I could not finish the
                    manuscript of my <rs type="work" ref="#tillich__IUGJQLWM">SYSTEMATIC THEOLOGY
                        vol. 1.</rs> which is due to the end of February. I believe that it is
                    better to postpone the review to the fall issue.<note type="ea"><rs
                            type="person" ref="#tillich_person_id__1928">Tillich</rs> liefert keine
                        Rezension zu den genannten Werken. In der Herbst-Ausgabe der Zeitschrift
                        findet sich jedoch eine Rezension zu <rs type="person"
                            ref="#tillich_person_id__5498">Cullmanns</rs>
                        <rs type="work" ref="#tillich__CG3UIZ3V">Christus und die Zeit</rs>. Vgl.
                            <rs type="person" ref="#tillich_person_id__2991">Amos N. Wilder</rs>:
                            <rs type="work" ref="#tillich__TEIPZGDH">Christ and Time: The Primitive
                            Christian Conception of Time and History by Oscar Cullmann</rs>
                        (1950).</note> I think <rs type="person" ref="#tillich_person_id__404">Mr.
                        Couch</rs> would agree with me in this decision. </p>
                <closer><salute>Sincerely yours,</salute><signed><rs type="person"
                            ref="#tillich_person_id__1928">Prof. Paul Tillich</rs></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
